WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.325
Access control should cover facilities, aircraft, controllers, applications, drone accounts,

00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:10.028
planning tools, data stores, dashboards, networks, backups, and exports.

00:00:10.028 --> 00:00:13.685
Use individual accounts, least privilege, strong authentication,

00:00:13.685 --> 00:00:16.820
and timely removal of stale access.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.000
Protect firmware and software through approved update, configuration,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.568
and vulnerability-management processes.

00:00:22.568 --> 00:00:25.703
Inventory versions and dependencies, review changes,

00:00:25.703 --> 00:00:30.406
and ensure crews are not quietly operating different configurations.

00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:34.063
Network security includes segmentation, secure remote access,

00:00:34.063 --> 00:00:38.243
monitored administrative activity, protected wireless services, secrets management,

00:00:38.243 --> 00:00:39.811
and controlled integrations.

00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:43.991
Avoid exposing management interfaces or sensitive telemetry unnecessarily.

00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:47.126
Privacy review begins at mission intake.

00:00:47.126 --> 00:00:53.396
Define purpose, area, detail, people affected, notice or consent where required, minimization,

00:00:53.396 --> 00:00:55.486
access, sharing, and retention.

00:00:55.486 --> 00:01:00.711
A legal flight can still create intrusive or disproportionate collection.

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:04.369
Audit logs and regulatory documentation support accountability.

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:09.072
Preserve approvals, qualifications, maintenance, flights, warnings, access, exports, incidents,

00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:15.864
and retention actions at a level appropriate to the operation and current requirements.

00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:20.044
Responsible-use policy prohibits harassment, stalking, unlawful surveillance, weaponization,

00:01:20.044 --> 00:01:24.224
restriction bypass, unsafe operations, and targeting private individuals.

00:01:24.224 --> 00:01:27.882
Compliance is not paperwork around the mission;

00:01:27.882 --> 00:01:32.585
it is the evidence that the program deserves trust.

00:01:32.585 --> 00:01:37.810
Third-party platforms and service providers belong in the security review.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.467
Evaluate data location, administrative access, retention, subcontractors,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.602
incident notification, export capability, account recovery,

00:01:44.602 --> 00:01:48.260
and what happens when the contract ends.
